course: dictionary
lesson: 12970
title: Exert: push, pull and effort
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Exert is one of these words. It is a verb, so it is something you do. Its forms are exert, exerts, exerted and exerting.
explain: «The magnet exerts a force on the iron nail.» Here exerts means pushes or pulls. The magnet is using its force on the nail. In science, you will often see the phrases exert a force and exert pressure.
explain: «Sam was so tired after the race that the doctor told him not to exert himself.» Here exert yourself means to make a big effort, with your body or your mind. The doctor is saying Sam should rest.
explain: «The team captain exerted a strong influence on the other players.» Here exert influence means to use your power to change how someone thinks or acts. When you meet exert, ask yourself: is something pushing or pulling, is someone working hard, or is someone using power?
fact: Exert means to push, pull or press with something.
fact: To exert yourself means to make a big physical or mental effort.
fact: To exert influence or control means to use your power to affect someone or something.
fact: «The Earth exerts a pull of gravity» on everything near it.
fact: Common phrases: exert a force, exert pressure, exert yourself, exert influence.
exercise: «The magnet exerts a force on the iron nail.» What does exerts mean here? | *Pushes or pulls with a force | Melts | Paints | Sleeps on
exercise: To exert yourself means to | Rest and do nothing at all | *Make a big physical or mental effort | Fall fast asleep | Sing very loudly
exercise: «The coach exerted her control over the team.» Find and copy the word that means used. | control | *exerted | team | coach
test: «Put your hand on the desk and you exert pressure on it.» What does exert pressure mean? | *Press down on something | Hide something | Wash the desk | Forget something
test: «The doctor said Mum must not exert herself after the operation.» What does this suggest? | Mum should eat more cake | Mum should shout loudly | Mum should run a marathon | *Mum should rest and avoid hard effort
exam: «Our captain's kindness exerted a calming influence on the whole team.» What does exerted mean here? | Gave away | *Used its power to affect | Stopped | Forgot
